title: "mss-agent: Meaning-Surplus-Security Framework — A Three-Layer Heat-Tax Architecture for LLM Conversation Quality"
version: 0.3.3
date-released: 2026-06-08
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20587900
repository-code: "https://github.com/mysama1/MSS-AI-Project"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/mss-agent/"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  MSS-Agent is an open-source Python framework that implements a three-layer
  architecture (L0 physical, L1 logical redundancy, L2 meaning integrity) for
  monitoring and constraining LLM conversations. It provides the Delta Protocol
  for detecting repetitive conversation patterns, HeatTax accounting for
  tracking meaning-waste budgets, and multi-agent orchestration with
  asyncio-based parallel execution and QuorumFast convergence detection.
keywords:
  - "LLM"
  - "AI safety"
  - "conversation quality"
  - "heat tax"
  - "multi-agent"
  - "open source"
  - "formal verification"
